# MOONSHOTS — Next-Generation Architectural Horizons (OODA 2.0, Metamorphic Binaries & Self-Healing Systems)

File: openOODA/MOONSHOTS.oot
This board tracks long-term paradigm shifts and architectural moonshots.
Roadmap board (ROADMAP.oot) focuses on current floor and active lane execution.

=== 1. OODA 2.0 & Sovereign Agentic Computing ===

[ ] Intent-Driven Swarm Synthesis
    Compile high-level natural language intent and formal capability/contract specifications directly
    into hyper-optimized SIMD/native assembly via multi-agent formal verification swarms.

[ ] Decentralized Capability Lattice & Verifiable Compute
    Pair SECRET field taint tracking with cryptographic ZK-STARK execution proofs.
    Execute code on untrusted decentralized cloud nodes with mathematical proof of contract compliance
    without revealing sensitive data in SECRET struct fields.

[ ] Pure .oo Microkernel & Hardware Sovereignty
    Bare-metal operating system kernel implemented entirely in .oo.
    Directly map hardware interrupts, device controllers, and MMU page tables to unforgeable capability tokens.

[ ] Sovereign Sandbox Fortresses
    Capability-sealed browser runtime unable to escape tokens or access host APIs without explicit user consent.
    Zero-trust package ecosystem and registry where dependencies cannot touch net or fs without main token grant.

=== 2. Metamorphic Binaries & Binary Transmutation ===

[ ] Automated Binary Transmutation & Telemetry Stripping
    Ingest foreign legacy binaries and packages (C/C++, Rust, Go, Zig, NPM, Homebrew).
    Statically trace call-graphs and concolic syscall reachability.
    Strip ambient tracking, telemetry, and ungranted network/filesystem access paths.
    Re-emit hardened native OODA binaries with unforgeable capability tokens and sealed interfaces.

[ ] Dynamic Metamorphic Compilation & Call-Edge Randomization
    Continuously morph memory layouts and function offsets across builds and execution cycles.
    Dynamic decoy padding (Path-A and Path-B) to prevent memory disclosure and ROP exploitation.
    Cryptographic Merkle hashing of valid call edges to eliminate unauthorized control flow hijacking.

[ ] Universal Holographic Poly-Binaries
    Single binary format that dynamically morphs execution across native CPU, confidential hardware
    enclaves (SGX/SEV/TrustZone), GPU/NPU tensor dispatch, and WASM sandboxes.

[ ] Bit-Identical Reproducible Builds
    Zero-timestamp, normalized AST digest output guaranteeing identical bit-for-bit binaries across all build environments.

=== 3. Self-Healing Systems & Autonomous Immune Regeneration ===

[ ] Autonomous Immune Regeneration (Self-Repairing Binaries)
    Fibers and actors execute within isolated micro-transactional memory bubbles (Undo-RAM/Merkle log).
    Zero-crash fault isolation: on contract violation, panic, or memory anomaly, rollback local state safely.
    Autonomously attenuate the offending capability and patch the routine in-memory without restarting.

[ ] Ghost-State Transactional Memory & Live Hot-Swap
    Speculative execution buffers that cancel and roll back state changes before commit upon invariant failure.
    Dynamically patch functions, traits, and struct definitions in a live running system with zero downtime.

[ ] Native Actors & Distributed Supervision Trees
    Scale beyond process-local queues to distributed, location-transparent actors with fault-tolerant supervision trees.

[ ] Struct-of-Arrays (SoA) / Data-Oriented Design (DoD) Auto-Emit
    Compiler automatically reorganizes struct layouts into cache-coherent contiguous vectors for high-throughput batch processing.

[ ] Compile-Time AST Macros in Product Expand
    Compile-time AST rewriting and domain-specific language expansions evaluated during pure product build.

[ ] Typestate Machine Verification
    Enforce compile-time protocol states (e.g. Unconnected -> Handshaking -> Authenticated -> Streaming) directly in the type system.
